    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰνίον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑν], τό, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴς
		Α</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>occipital bone,
				occiput</i>, [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ τριχωτοῦ κρανίου] . . τὸ ὀπίσθιον
					[ἐστὶν] ἰνίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					491a33
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				9.17
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεφαλῆς κατὰ ἰνίον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.73
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ ἰνίου ἦλθεν [δόρυ</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				14.495
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				3.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecyd.
				66
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.264
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Euph.
				41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Mar.</u>
				33
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ-</span> codd., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἰν-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
				</span></i>
			 l.c., but cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφινίους: τὰς ἐπὶ
				τοῦ ἰνίου σάρκας</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>)</div>
